  "id": "bounded-rationality",
  "term": "bounded rationality",
  "definition": "Bounded rationality is the idea that people do not always make fully rational decisions because their access to information, ability to process it, and psychological biases are limited. In practice, complex information, emotions, and expectations can lead judgments away from strictly rational choices.",
